  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Wasn't sure what category to ask this in, but was there any specific reason why dynamic bones worked by moving the position of the child bone, and VRChat chose to make physbones work by moving the rotation of the parent bone?\n\nconsidering the confliction when the bone rotation is already animated example by humanoid animations, hence why we cant have physbones on humanoid bones anymore, I want to know VRChat's logic behind that choice to use rotation instead of position. Was it a lawsuit kind of thing if they followed dynamic bone to closely? Or was there a different reason? Just seems a bit strange and frustrating.",
